{
  "dom_id": "step-9289",
  "name": "Example: \n                    Identifying True Statements Given Some Polyhedra Nets",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14248692/assets/e427a98c2953792d799190b7fc20a7dbf12ce014655316e21fb809e0abc9cdc5.png)\n\nWhich of the statements is true about the solids shown above?\n\nI. The net of solid I consists of triangles only.\n\nII. The net of solid II consists of $4$ triangles and $2$ rectangles.\n\nIII. The net of solid III consists of triangles only.",
  "worked_solution": "Let's sketch the net of each solid.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14248692/assets/023f11b6924e6cf7318f54f5acdf910b1f688ee8ac40ec8f3b3ab7cd9c13c8df.png)\n\n \n\nNow, let's go through the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is false because the net of solid I consists of rectangles.\n\n- Statement II is false because the net of solid II consists of $2$ triangles and $3$ rectangles.\n\n- Statement III is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"",
